WEBVTT

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:03.960
Special Announcement!
Tatsuo, 54 Years Old
Falls in Love, Laments to Love

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.460
As an editor, the most rewarding moment
is when something I've worked on

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.460
Author Miyoshi Natsume's "54"
The Hit Serial Finally Released
All-in-One Hardcover Book Announced!

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.340
is compiled for a major release.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.620
I want to help spread
as many copies into the world as I can.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.790
Oh, the person in charge of "54"?

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.670
Book Sales Department

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.420
It's Chiba.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.830
I want to put it in the hands
of as many people as possible.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.340
Chiba-kun!

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:52.010
A man who can work, that's the type she likes

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:56.290
I psyched myself up and got down to business

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.870
But I'm always so busy and so bored

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.540
The company I work at now is pretty high level

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.710
And my dad has a lot of connections there

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.870
So there's no way I can quit

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.290
I'm always all by myself

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:33.460
I just take a bath and fall asleep

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:38.880
I can't even take the time to admire

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:45.300
Your hair or the way you walk

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:50.630
If all I can do is sleep

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:56.880
Then at least in my dreams

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.880
I want to see you

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.870
Reward Man

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.250
Only 20,000?!

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.420
That's not nearly enough!

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.420
No, actually that's on the high end.
We're going out on a limb, so be grateful.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:20.460
I mean, if you consider that 10,000 is the average
for a first press, then sure, it's a lot...

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.500
But Natsume-sensei has...

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.920
The book she released last year had 50,000 copies
printed... but only sold about 67% of that.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.500
Which means that, in actuality,
her sales numbers average out to about 30,000.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.170
That's the number we came to when
I talked it over with my boss,

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.210
and I personally think 20,000 is plenty.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.130
You've been totally brainwashed by being in sales.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.340
I suppose.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:51.160
Unlike you folks in editorial,
those of us in sales tend to be realists.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.830
Well, you've only ever worked
with magazines, Matsukata,

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.910
so you don't understand the intricacies of books.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:01.460
If we print too many and the stores end up
returning them, then it puts us in a tough spot.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.670
You're the one who doesn't understand!

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.800
"54" is the most popular piece
in our magazine right now!

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.010
It's become more popular
than anything else we've ever printed!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.500
People will buy copies by the truckload
if you just print them, I can feel it!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.960
I'm telling you a boom is coming!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.010
I get it! I hear you, so please
stop spitting rice all over me.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.250
Out of all things, why did you pick
a natto roll to eat for lunch, anyway?

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.130
Right back at you.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:27.920
Huh?

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.620
It's all over your face...
the meat sauce from your lunch.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.510
"I can feel it"... "A boom is coming"...

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.790
None of that is concrete proof,
so it's completely unreliable to me.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.760
As much as I hate to say it.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.250
Editors usually have an emotional attachment
to their work, which is why...

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.920
they always overestimate
the number of copies necessary.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.500
Dealing with those numbers more realistically

00:03:54.460 --> 00:04:00.790
Makoto Chiba (28)
Employee at Gotansha Publishing Inc. - Book Sales Department

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.960
is our job in the sales department.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.870
We get a lot of flack for it.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.460
I'm sorry.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.500
I tried my best, but everyone
has already made up their minds.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.000
So the first press will only be 20,000 copies...

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.880
Ah... okay.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.880
I'm really sorry!

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:13.880
I wasn't convincing enough!

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.800
No, you've done more than enough.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.670
Don't worry! It will definitely get an additional print!

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.050
No, that's okay.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:23.090
"54" is a boom waiting to happen.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.670
I can already picture the faces of those jerks in
sales when it sells out and they panic to print more!

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.380
How can I help you?

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.630
Thank you and come again!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.500
Thank you!

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.750
Good afternoon! My name is Chiba
from Gotansha Publishing.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.540
Is your manager, Fujita, in today?

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.120
Oh, hello there, Chiba-san!

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:48.670
Hello!

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:50.710
Always a pleasure to do business with you.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.500
Well business has been booming lately!

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.000
Particularly Koganezawa-sensei's
"Party of Darkness 4: Knock Your Socks Off"!

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:58.410
That series has been selling
more and more with each volume.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.500
The next installment will be ready
to hit shelves by next month!

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.790
Great! Then we'd like to put in a large order.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.460
Thank you very much!

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.290
Huh?

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:10.630
No More Aimless Love For Me
Miyoshi Natsume

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.370
Natsume-sensei's books...

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.620
Last time I was here,
you just had them on the shelves, right?

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:11.670
Yeah.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.040
But lately they've really been moving out the door.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.000
That serial your company is publishing, "54,"
has been getting a lot of buzz lately.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.750
As you can see, even men
have started to buy her older books.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.750
So I decided to try moving them out of the women's
section and into the main area for everyone.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.370
Oh?

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.170
I'm telling you a boom is coming!

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:30.920
No More Aimless Love For Me

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.250
Thank you very much.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.540
Would you like a book cover for it?

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.090
Oh! "54" will actually go on sale
in hardcover next month.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.370
Really?

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:41.800
Please consider placing an order.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.630
Just between you and me...

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.790
I'm actually really looking forward to it!

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:46.500
Huh?

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.000
I find the main character to be very relatable,
if you know what I mean.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.300
Really?

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.290
Are you telling me you're in
a similar situation, Fujita-san?

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:58.460
A forlorn old man finding true love, just maybe!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.540
Is that so? Then you're really living the dream!

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.590
Assure everything goes as smooth as possible.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.250
A fundamental part of making sales.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:09.710
And in order to make sure
that all interactions go smoothly...

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.290
any quips and reactions to jokes
must be equally as smooth.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.120
Sincerity is not necessary.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.300
All we have to do is avoid losses to the company.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:20.790
And stay focused on moving

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:24.250
Author Miyoshi Natsume's "54" Hardcover
All-in-One Coming Soon! Re-experience
the Heartbreaking Love Story of the 54-year-old Tatsuo!

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.200
the products out to retailers.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.170
I skimmed through when
JIDAI started publishing it...

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.500
but I haven't read the whole thing properly.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:34.710
Author Miyoshi Natsume's "54" Hardcover
All-in-One Coming Soon!
Re-experience the Heartbreaking Love Story
of the 54-year-old Tatsuo!

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:34.500
The main character is a cheating
old man named... Tatsuo, that's right.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:38.750
He has the same name... as my old man.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:44.710
I don't let myself get emotionally attached
to books that I work with.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.590
Because four years ago...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.630
I got emotionally attached to a certain book.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:54.830
Proven Method!
"Become a Billionaire in 5 Minutes"
All the Secrets Revealed!!

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:54.420
It was just one of those
everyday "how-to" books, but...

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:57.250
A woman I really liked was involved with it.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.500
I ran around to every bookstore I could find.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.300
Created promotional materials.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:03.750
Wrote advertisements.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.710
Did everything I possibly could.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:09.340
Proven Method!
"Become a Billionaire in 5 Minutes"
All the Secrets Revealed!!

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.210
And it sold!

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.290
It sold big time!

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:10.830
We did it!

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:12.880
It made the best sellers!

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:18.000
Proven Method! "Become a Billionaire in 5 Minutes"
All the Secrets Revealed!!

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:17.960
At the very least, I felt that my contributions
had been a significant part of its success.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.460
That book sold really well,
"Become a Billionaire in 5 Minutes"!

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.460
There's going to be an additional printing,
they said. That's amazing!

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.960
Well, you know... all that work I put in
with the writer really paid off!

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.880
It made me so angry...

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:43.550
I was so pissed off at myself...
for expecting anything more.

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:51.290
My name is Chiba, I was in charge
of pushing sales for your book.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:52.960
Ah... hello.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.460
Furukawa-san!

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:55.130
Oh!

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.630
Come on, everyone is waiting!

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.540
Furukawa-san, congratulations!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.500
No, it's nothing. This was all thanks
to your hard work.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.460
How stupid am I?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:16.590
Did you just expect to get a reward...
like some kind of puppy?

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.410
Idiot...

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:32.830
Read it.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.420
Is that the proof copy?

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:37.880
No. That isn't finished yet,
so I just printed a copy from our data.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.000
I made the cover myself. Just give it a read!

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.790
Wait, I told you I already read some
when it was published in JIDAI.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.000
Take it!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.540
You need to have a little
more appreciation for this book!

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.040
Then you can sell it!

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.290
Now listen...

00:08:56.710 --> 00:09:01.130
I told you, if we got attached to every single book
we sold, then we couldn't do our jobs properly.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.080
We have a lot of books to sell.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:07.170
Besides, I'm free to decide which books
I want to invest myself in or not, right?

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.120
What right do you have to tell me
which books I should appreciate?

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.040
I don't...

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.050
Exactly.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.000
But, you should still read it!

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.920
Afterwards you can decide
whether you want to be invested or not!

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.840
Mouth. Meat sauce.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:42.880
Here.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:43.760
Thank you.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.800
So that's why I want the guys in sales to understand

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:49.170
the feelings of those of us on the frontlines.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:51.920
So, what about your department?

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:55.370
Do they all understand
how the people in sales feel?

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.250
Huh?

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.750
Have you ever thought about what
the sales department goes through?

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.330
They also have their own frontlines to fight on.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.290
What...?

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.420
Oh, thank you.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.500
Hello, this is Yamashiro.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.920
Ah, thanks for all of your help.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.880
Oh, regarding that...

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:32.210
Yes... that's right... I'll make sure
they get the message in the morning.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:34.410
I'm very sorry about that.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.840
Chiba: Visiting bookstores till 2PM

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.330
I'll be back before today's departmental meeting.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.250
Alright.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:55.500
I've heard people say that he was
one of the most talented salesmen...

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.670
...but he's really changed... Chiba-kun.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.830
Anyone would change after spending
5 years at one company.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.040
He has a severe attitude problem.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.120
Well... he told me once...

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:11.960
In the beginning, he was
REALLY invested in his work.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:15.040
But ultimately that came back
to bite him pretty hard.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.880
So he's trying to change that.

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:18.960
"Change"...?

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.800
Not getting too personally attached,
or something like that.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.670
Is that true?

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:24.380
Yeah.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.010
At least, that's what I heard.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:34.550
Damn it... this is really good!

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.590
I don't want my best efforts
to get betrayed in the end.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.300
I don't want... to feel hatred towards anyone.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:46.960
Don't get attached.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:51.960
Don't go the extra mile.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.420
Be flat.

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.660
In the end, that is the best method to make sure...

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:59.170
that everything goes smoothly.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:05.960
You made a sign to promote the release?

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.630
Miyoshi Natsume,
The author of JIDAI's Hit Serial "54"!
Get Her Other Books Before They're Gone!

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:08.920
Yeah. I know these were published
by a different company, but...

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:13.420
Honestly, we keep getting too many questions
about the release date for "54."

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.920
The number of people buying
her other books just keeps increasing.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.090
We ordered more copies of these two here.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.540
No More Aimless Love for Me
Knock on the Heart
Miyoshi Natsume
Miyoshi Natsume

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:20.750
Now we're waiting on the next print.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.040
I have to do something to keep my spirits up.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:30.420
Actually... that woman I mentioned to you before...

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.250
She... cut off contact with me recently.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.130
The woman you mentioned before...?

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:41.550
I told you last time that I really related to Tatsuo...
the protagonist of "54," remember?

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:43.670
Oh!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:48.050
Honestly, at this point "54"
could almost be my biography.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:53.840
I thought that was just a joke during our little chat...

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.260
"Expecting" or "feeling" a boom...

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:00.000
That's just an illusion created
by the editor's personal attachment.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:04.000
Such personal attachments
are unfit for a salesman.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.710
Or so I thought...

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.080
But...!

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:15.840
Books which elicit that kind of response
can result in action that may help move sales!

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.080
No, that will definitely move sales!

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.420
In truth, I...

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.250
knew that all along!

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:27.590
Meeting in Progress

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:27.960
In regards to the first press numbers for "54"...

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.750
I think we should print 50,000 copies.

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:32.250
Huh? I thought we agreed on 20,000.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.710
Yes, but I think we should increase that to 50,000.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.750
Natsume-san doesn't really have
any male readership, right?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:40.630
No...

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:45.540
But the serial published in our magazine has
become really popular, so I think it would be good.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.790
Exactly.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:51.630
But we can't tell whether the book
will actually sell or not just based on that.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.210
I suppose so.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:57.630
There's also no guarantee her female readers
will stay with her for this release.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:13:59.840
But...

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:04.340
I've visited multiple bookstores and noticed
her work is being prominently displayed.

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:07.330
And some stores have even created
their own signage for her.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.380
Miyoshi Natsume,
The author of JIDAI's Hit Serial "54"!
Get Her Other Books Before They're Gone!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:10.460
Just because you saw that
in a few bookstores around here

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:12.540
doesn't mean it's true for the whole country.

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.300
Of course, I can't deny that.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:20.960
Besides, from looking at the data we already know,
her sales numbers have been dropping every year.

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:24.790
She's losing steam.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.040
Why print more copies?

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:29.920
I keep telling you...

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.670
Don't get caught up in the fervor.

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.250
Keep a clear head when you make decisions.

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:44.620
There's not enough demand for us
to print 50,000 copies.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.790
20,000 is more than enough, right?

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.500
Yeah... I suppose so.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.500
There will be a demand!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:06.960
And I'm fully prepared to carefully explain to you
all the reasons I know that to be the case.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:11.120
Keep it short.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:15.540
I've already decided that I'm in agreement with him.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.050
Ah, I'm exhausted...

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.000
Why did I get dragged into all that?

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:28.210
You know I just want to say, that's what the world calls love

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:26.960
Matsukata!

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.380
Yes?

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.130
The first press number for "54"

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.420
got raised to 40,000 copies.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:34.580
WHAT?! No way!

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:38.120
If even a faint glow shines from within those tears

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.660
Why? That's double what it was!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.620
Well... that friend of yours... Chiba, was it?

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:45.500
I'll tell you that they warmed me up as I stood in front of you

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:41.670
Yes.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:46.170
He was at the meeting... and made
a really passionate argument for over 3 hours.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:51.960
But even then, our voices will just dry out in the end

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:49.330
Eventually the sales department manager,
Kaneko, gave in to him.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:50.000
Huh?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:54.550
Well, personally speaking, I don't hate
persistent guys like him. Actually...

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.420
So before morning comes,

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:58.590
H-hey! I wasn't done talking to you yet!

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:59.550
I'd at least like to sing with someone

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:06.750
If yesterday you were only an imitation

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.580
Chiba-kun actually... Chiba-kun actually did it!
He fought for us!

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:13.120
Then I just have to leave the view from yesterday behind

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:10.580
Coming.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:15.130
Excuse the late visit! I wanted to be able
to tell you this in person...

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:19.420
What brings a new day is a new you and me

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.500
40,000! It's 40,000!

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:18.630
Huh?

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:22.580
The first press order for "54" was doubled,
it's 40,000 now!

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:23.130
Somehow we understand each other

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.040
Doubled? Can that really happen?

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:26.540
That's what the world calls love

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.000
Yes.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:32.880
I never knew letting the heart speak could be so terrifying

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:31.920
A man in our sales department named Chiba
worked really hard on our behalf during a meeting.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:36.630
You and I tune our voices to each other

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.300
Chiba-san in sales...?

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.630
I've never met him before...

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:44.460
And sing as if everything in the past never happened

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.590
And this is the first time I've even heard his name...

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:42.250
So why did he...?

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:43.580
Sensei...

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:48.050
Most people in sales never meet
with the authors directly.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:53.040
There will come a day when we lose faith in someone

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.340
Of course, that's just the nature of their job.

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:54.620
But, if they don't get out there
and push sales for us...

00:16:53.580 --> 00:17:00.410
For now let's at least sing a beautiful song

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.500
then the stores wouldn't carry our books!

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:06.090
If we only used sad words, oh yeah

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:05.210
It's out.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.420
It's finally out!

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.590
The day has come!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.290
Nothing would ever change

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.380
Hello?

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:14.210
Who care what those jerks did

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.010
Oh, is this Chiba-san?

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.460
We sold out of "54" almost immediately!

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:21.250
If yesterday you were a betrayer

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.460
What?

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.630
We'd like to order another 50 copies!

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:22.210
Hello? Chiba-san? Can you hear me?

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:27.500
Then I just have to forget the view from yesterday

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.590
Ah... yes, I heard you!

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.500
Yes, that's right! Order another printing!

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:33.710
What brings a new day is love that's almost too sweet

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.790
50,000? That's not enough.

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:31.000
Make it 70,000!

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:37.250
We make sense of it together

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:36.960
Hello, Chiba-san?

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:39.840
We'd like to order another 30 copies
as soon as possible!
That's also what the world calls love

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:40.790
Currently
out of
stock!

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:41.130
That's also what the world calls love

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:47.210
I never knew letting the heart speak could be so terrifying

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:42.250
60 more, please!

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.510
Matsukata!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.250
Second printing of 90,000 is on the way!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:50.920
Somehow our voices tune to each other

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.590
For real?!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:59.630
And sing as if everything in the past never happened

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:54.080
Roger that!

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.290
WE DID IT!

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.210
Miyoshi Natsume's "54" Now on Sale!

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.710
Excuse me, do you have "54"?

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:07.130
I'm very sorry. We're currently waiting
on a new shipment to arrive.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.800
Restock Expected
Mid November

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.550
Top 10 Best Sellers For
"54" by Miyoshi Natsume

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:18.590
"54"
Celebration Party
Over 540,000 copies sold

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:24.870
"54" has sold over 540,000 copies! Congratulations!

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:26.630
Cheers!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.370
Cheers!

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.000
Thank you so much.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.750
I owe so, so much to everyone here.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.660
Sensei... this is such great news!

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:41.050
Thank you, Nagisa-san!

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.870
Can I get your autograph on my copy?

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:43.870
Of course.

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:47.880
Someday, I'll be the one to...

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.750
To Mayu Nagisa
All my thanks.

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:53.130
Nobody needs to know.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:57.960
If the book sells well... that's all that matters.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:04.170
Sensei! This is Chiba from our sales department.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.170
I apologize for not introducing myself earlier.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:14.250
I'm Chiba, and I was the salesman
in charge of pushing your new book.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.090
Ah! So you're the one!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:16.960
Huh?

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:22.210
Um... thank you so very much
for working hard to sell my book.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:26.130
It's nothing...

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:28.420
Thank you, please excuse me.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:33.040
Natsume-sensei! May we take your picture?

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:33.870
Of course!

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.460
Chiba-kun!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:59.920
I never expected that I would actually...
get real gratitude from an author.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:02.670
I'm happy...

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:07.460
So happy...

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.960
We're all happy!

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:27.750
Here.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.750
They had the meat sauce you like.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.080
Thanks.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.340
As an editor...

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:40.090
one of the most rewarding moments
is when something you've worked on

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.410
gets compiled into a major release.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.580
I wonder what the most rewarding moment
is for those in sales?

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:47.960
Is it when the book sells really well?

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:50.420
Or is it...

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:56.160
You've got sauce... all over your mouth.

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:04.710
Later... I think I'll ask Chiba-kun what he thinks.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.380
Shangri-la

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:37.590
Even in my dreams you can't manage a proper smile

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:42.910
I just want to chide and love a hopeless person like you

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:49.920
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:53.500
Where shall we go?

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:58.960
Ahh... ahh...

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:02.210
Shangri-la

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:06.170
Let me hear you shout "I'm happy!"

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:10.460
Let me see the tears underneath your tough exterior

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:12.130
Shangri-la

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:17.090
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:22.120
Please chide and love a hopeless person like me

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:25.380
Shinji
Nice Work Today
Do your best, but don't
wear yourself out.
-Shinji

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:35.710
Next Episode: Accomplished Hataraki Man
